{
  "id": "Lyo.Reporting.Api",
  "name": "Lyo.Reporting.Api",
  "area": "Apps",
  "tagline": "Authenticated HTTP endpoints for Lyo Reporting. Postgres stays service-only (`ReportService` + EF). `BuildReportingGroup` lives in this package.",
  "description": "Authenticated HTTP endpoints for Lyo Reporting. Postgres stays service-only (`ReportService` + EF). `BuildReportingGroup` lives in this package.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Set up the host",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "// One call registers Postgres management (DbContext factory, migrations, CRUD services,\n// CSV/XLSX/JSON renderers, ReportService, retention, throttle) plus the API export contributor.\n// Equivalent to AddPostgresReportingManagement + AddLyoApiReporting.\nservices.AddReportingApi(o => {\n    o.ConnectionString = cs;\n    o.EnableAutoMigrations = true;\n});\n// Or bind from appsettings (\"PostgresReporting\" section by default):\n// services.AddReportingApiFromConfiguration(builder.Configuration);\n\nservices.AddReportingMaintenanceWorker(); // optional retention cleanup + stuck-run sweeper\nservices.AddReportingWebRenderer(); // optional HTML/PDF\nservices.AddReportDataProvider<MyReportDataProvider>();\nservices.AddReportingGenerationProfile(\"email-client-message\", p => p\n    .DefaultFormat(ReportFormat.Csv)\n    .DefaultFileName(\"report.csv\")\n    .DefaultPathPrefix(\"reports/email\"));\n\n// Worker / Discord policy example:\nservices.AddAuthorization(o => {\n    o.AddPolicy(\"ReportingGenerate\", p => p.RequireAuthenticatedUser());\n});\n\nvar app = builder.Build();\napp.BuildReportingGroup(new ReportingApiOptions {\n    DefinitionAuth = EndpointAuth.RequireAuthenticatedUser(),\n    GenerationAuth = EndpointAuth.RequireAuthenticatedUser(),\n    GenerateAuth = EndpointAuth.RequireAuthorization(\"ReportingGenerate\"),\n    DownloadAuth = EndpointAuth.RequireAuthenticatedUser(),\n    // Download endpoint is only mapped when this factory is set:\n    DownloadStreamFactory = (ctx, ct) => {\n        var storage = ctx.Services.GetRequiredService<IFileStorageService>();\n        return storage.GetFileStreamAsync(ctx.OutputFileId, ct: ct);\n    }\n});"
    },
    {
      "title": "How a worker calls it",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "await reporting.Generations.GenerateAsync(new GenerateReportReq {\n    ReportDefinitionId = definitionId,\n    Parameters = [new() { Key = \"ClientId\", Type = LyoTypeInfo.Guid.FullName, Value = LyoTypeInfo.Guid.ToJson(clientId) }],\n    Format = ReportFormat.Csv\n});\n\n// Re-run a past generation and stream its output:\nvar rerun = await reporting.Generations.RerunAsync(generationId);\nvar (stream, fileName, length) = await reporting.Generations.DownloadAsync(rerun.Id);"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Authorization matrix",
      "headers": [
        "Surface",
        "Options property",
        "Endpoints"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Definitions",
          "`DefinitionAuth`",
          "Export + CRUD"
        ],
        [
          "Parameters on a definition",
          "`DefinitionAuth`",
          "CRUD under `Reporting/Definition/Parameter`"
        ],
        [
          "Generations",
          "`GenerationAuth`",
          "Get / Query / Delete / DeleteBulk (include `Parameters`). Delete runs `OnCleanupAsync` so persisted output is removed from storage."
        ],
        [
          "Generate",
          "`GenerateAuth`",
          "`POST Reporting/Generation/Generate` (`Parameters` list in the body)"
        ],
        [
          "Resolve parameter Options",
          "`DefinitionAuth`",
          "`POST Reporting/ResolveParameterOptions` (Sproc/Query picker rows for the workbench; not a public execute-any-sproc API)"
        ],
        [
          "Rerun",
          "`GenerateAuth`",
          "`POST Reporting/Generation/{id}/Rerun`"
        ],
        [
          "Download",
          "`DownloadAuth`",
          "`GET Reporting/Generation/{id}/Download` (mapped only when `DownloadStreamFactory` is set)"
        ]
      ],
      "trail": "If every auth slot shares one policy, prefer `ReportingApiOptions.WithAuth(auth, downloadStreamFactory)` over setting all four properties.\n\nAll auth slots default to `EndpointAuth.RequireAuthorization()` (authenticated user). **Breaking change:** previously the defaults were `null` (endpoint fell through to the\nbuilder/host default); anonymous access now requires an explicit `EndpointAuth.Anonymous()` per slot. Setting a property to `null` restores the old fall-through behavior, but\nprefer explicit values for Worker and Discord hosts."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "CreatedBy",
      "text": "The authenticated identity always wins: `GenerateReportReq.CreatedBy` is overwritten with `User.Identity.Name` when the caller is authenticated. Client-supplied `CreatedBy` is only honored for unauthenticated/service callers, falling back to `\"Unknown\"`."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "title": "HTTP status codes",
      "items": [
        "Validation failures (`ReportValidationException`: unknown keys, bad parameters, malformed/oversized JSON, inactive or missing definition, ad-hoc disabled) → **400** ProblemDetails.",
        "Concurrency saturation (`ReportBusyException`, see `PostgresReportingOptions.MaxConcurrentGenerations`) → **503** ProblemDetails.",
        "Download: **404** when the generation or blob is missing, **409** when the generation has no downloadable output (not `Succeeded` or no `OutputFileId`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "title": "Validating definition writes",
      "items": [
        "`ReportDataJson` must parse as JSON and stay under `MaxReportDataJsonBytes`.",
        "Parameter `Type` and `DefaultFormat` must be valid enum values.",
        "`ValidationRegex` must compile (1s timeout) and stay within the 500-char cap.",
        "`MaxLength`/`MinLength` must be non-negative and coherent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Protecting sensitive fields",
      "text": "`QueryProject` and projected `Export` read raw entities and skip the response mapper's masking, so reporting endpoints deny selecting `Value`/`EncryptedValue` on parameter paths (including nested paths like `Parameters.EncryptedValue` and computed-field templates) via `DeniedSelectFields`. `Get`/`QueryConcrete` map through the response types, which mask parameter values (`***` for encrypted-backed values, `EncryptedValue` never returned)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Cleanup when a definition is deleted",
      "text": "Deleting a definition cascades its generation rows. Before the delete, `ReportGenerationHooks.OnCleanupAsync` runs for each generation with an `OutputFileId` so the persisted blob can be removed; a hook failure aborts the delete rather than orphaning storage."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "How a worker calls it",
      "body": "Workers call `IReportingClient.Generations.GenerateAsync` with a bearer token that satisfies `GenerateAuth`:\n\n\n\nFileStorage hooks, renderers, and data providers run on the API host. Not in the worker process."
    }
  ],
